      "5": [
        "round down if you end up with a fraction"
      ],
      "12": [
        "It isn’t a building or a vehicle",
        "if riding horses or other mounts, the group can move twice that distance for 1 hour",
        "Travelers in wagons, carriages, or other land vehicles choose a pace as normal",
        "Characters in a waterborne vessel are limited to the speed of the vessel, and they don’t choose a travel pace",
        "ships might be able to travel for up to 24 hours per day"
      ],
      "15": [
        "A willing creature that is at least one size larger than a rider and that has an appropriate anatomy can serve as a mount",
        "Doing so costs an amount of movement equal to half your Speed (round down)"
      ],
      "16": [
        "You can control a mount only if it has been trained to accept a rider",
        "it has only three action options during that turn: Dash, Disengage, and Dodge",
        "you must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw or fall off",
        "While mounted, you must make the same save if you’re knocked Prone or the mount is",
        "down to 0, which is the lowest Hit Points can go"
      ],
      "92": [
        "Chain Mail 16 Str 13 Disadvantage 55 lb. 75 GP",
        "Leather Armor 11 + Dex modifier — — 10 lb. 10 GP"
      ],
      "100": [
        "its primary purpose is to carry gear that would otherwise slow you down",
        "can move weight up to five times its base carrying capacity, including the weight of the vehicle",
        "If multiple animals pull the same vehicle, add their carrying capacities together",
        "The cost is four times the normal cost, and it weighs twice as much",
        "A Military Saddle gives Advantage on any ability check you make to remain mounted",
        "An Exotic Saddle is required for riding an aquatic or a flying mount",
        "A ship sailing against a strong wind moves at half speed",
        "waterborne ships can’t move under sail and must be rowed",
        "add the speed of the current (typically 3 miles per hour) to the speed of the vehicle",
        "they can be pulled upstream by draft animals on the shores",
        "A Rowboat can be carried and weighs 100 pounds"
      ],
      "101": [
        "A ship larger than a Keelboat or Rowboat needs a crew of skilled hirelings",
        "can carry one-fifth as many passengers",
        "usually pays 5 SP per day for a hammock",
        "A small private cabin usually costs 2 GP per day",
        "If a vehicle has a damage threshold",
        "Repairs to a damaged ship can be made while the vessel is berthed",
        "Repairing 1 Hit Point of damage requires 1 day and costs 20 GP for materials and labor",
        "the repair time and cost are halved"
      ],
      "102": [
        "Skilled hireling 2 GP per day"
      ],
      "180": [
        "equal to or greater than its damage threshold, in which case it takes that entire instance of damage"
      ],
      "192": [
        "Characters traveling in a vehicle use the vehicle’s speed in miles per hour"
      ],
      "360": [
        "Riding Horse"
      ]
    },
